@startuml
title Runenwerk networking architecture (post-RN8)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
left to right direction

package "apps / preview integration" {
  [Runenwerk Editor Preview Client] as preview_client
  [Runtime Preview Host] as preview_host
}

package "engine integration" {
  [Application / Session Lifecycle] as engine_session
  [RunenNet Session Projection] as session_projection
  [Net Wire + Driver Contracts] as engine_contracts
  [Replication + Prediction Systems] as engine_replication
  [Replication I/O Staging] as engine_io
  [Replay Systems] as engine_replay
}

package "external RunenNet" {
  [runen-net Core] as runennet_core
  [runen-net-quic] as runennet_quic
}

package "net (Runenwerk support)" {
  package "engine_sim" {
    [simulation vocabulary] as sim
  }

  package "engine_history" {
    [replay / archive / validation] as history
  }
}

preview_client --> runennet_quic : preview control client
preview_host --> runennet_quic : preview control server
runennet_quic --> runennet_core

engine_session --> runennet_core : negotiation + session lifecycle
engine_session --> session_projection : accepted bindings only
session_projection --> engine_replication : authorized connections
engine_replication --> runennet_core : replication / input / prediction semantics
engine_replication --> engine_contracts : encode / decode / envelope formation
engine_io --> engine_contracts : staged messages
engine_contracts --> sim
engine_replay --> history
history --> sim

note right of runennet_core
Standalone RunenNet is the sole reusable
connection/session/delivery/replication/prediction
semantic authority.
end note

note right of engine_contracts
Runenwerk-owned integration DTOs and gameplay
driver traits only. No duplicate session,
history, recovery, or prediction authority.
end note

note right of engine_io
Engine work queues are staging only.
Queue admission is not DeliveryAcceptance.
end note

note right of runennet_quic
Concrete QUIC exists only where selected
by a maintained consumer.
end note

@enduml
